    "specPath": "specs/109-governed-harness/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "The harness is what an agent may do in this repository, so it is claimed by a spec and held by the coupling gate. This spec adopts the spec-spine Claude Code kit (spec-spine 0.18.0, kit spec 082): ten repository-invariant skills forming the governed loop, four pipeline agents carrying this repo's project layer, four rules, the read-only hook set, a Makefile whose `make gate` is the one definition of the gate that CI and every session run, and the pin that refuses an older binary. It replaces the hand-copied five-skill harness that predated `spec-spine check`, and turns on the ownership ratchet now that every source file is specifically claimed.\n",
    "title": "Governed harness: the spec-spine kit as the loop this repo runs"
